  description: 'Adversarial audit of the entire brain viz PR: 7 review dimensions, each finding verified',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Review', detail: '7 dimensions review the viz feature in parallel' },
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'adversarially verify each finding — refute or confirm' },
  ],
}

const ROOT = args.root
const CTX = `You are auditing a PR that adds \`entire brain viz\` to the Go module github.com/ashtom/entire-brain.
It is a LOCAL, LOOPBACK-ONLY, NO-EGRESS web interface that renders a repo's "brain" (semantic code graph,
facts, history, sessions, docs) as a Canvas2D force-directed graph. Hard invariants that MUST hold:
- Binds 127.0.0.1 ONLY (never 0.0.0.0). Read-only disk reads. No outbound network of any kind.
- Self-contained embedded SPA (go:embed webui/dist), no CDN/external fetch; a CSP header enforces this.
Files (all under ${ROOT}):
- internal/cli/viz.go      (backend: cobra cmd, http mux, JSON handlers, graph/replay builders)
- internal/cli/viz_test.go (httptest handler tests)
- internal/cli/root.go     (one-line command registration)
- webui.go                 (module-root go:embed of webui/dist)
- webui/dist/app.js        (router + fetch + wiring + audio + slider + replay)
- webui/dist/graph.js      (force sim + Canvas2D renderer)
- webui/dist/index.html, style.css, logo.svg, symbol.svg
Read the actual files. Reason from the real code. Do NOT run mutating builds/tests (a shared worktree);
static analysis + read-only grep only. For every issue construct the CONCRETE trigger before claiming it.
Report ONLY real defects in THIS PR's code — not pre-existing repo issues, not style nits unless they cause bugs.`

const FINDINGS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  additionalProperties: false,
  required: ['findings'],
