// GRACE PERIOD: an in-flight publish's object is always young (written before
// its pointer commits), so never reap a young object. Skipping here is what
// defeats both the first-publish and overwrite races — the just-written object
// is caught by a later run once it is old enough to prove no longer in flight.
// An unknown (zero) ModTime is treated as YOUNG and skipped: age is the sole
// grace guard, so an object whose age we cannot establish must fail CLOSED
// (never reaped) rather than fail open into the pre-grace data-loss race.
if obj.ModTime.IsZero() || now.Sub(obj.ModTime) < minAge {
	continue
