// ObjectMeta is one physical object returned by ListWithMeta: its key and the
// last time the object bytes were written (its S3 LastModified). ModTime is the
// object's AGE source — the absence-of-reference GC uses it to enforce a grace
// period so an in-flight publish's freshly written (young) object is never
// mistaken for an orphan and reaped. A zero ModTime means the backend reported
// no timestamp; the GC treats such an object as arbitrarily old (never
// grace-protected), so a backend that omits the field degrades to the
// pre-grace behaviour rather than silently protecting everything forever.

