The fix: interface method DeleteRefAndCount(repoKey,branch,ref)(remaining,err) — deletes THIS (repoKey,branch,ref) row then returns count of rows still referencing (repoKey,ref) across OTHER branches, atomically. Mem: delete+count under one mutex. Pg: one tx doing SELECT 1 ... WHERE repo_key AND overlay_ref ORDER BY branch FOR UPDATE, then DELETE this row, then SELECT count(*). GCOverlays: snapshot refs; per ref DeleteRefAndCount; err→return without shred (fail-safe); remaining>0→skip (sibling owns it); remaining==0→enc.Shred. Blanket Delete removed. Migration 028 gained a (repo_key, overlay_ref) index.
