const LENSES = [
  { key:'concurrency', prompt:`LENS: the concurrency correctness of DeleteRefAndCount + shred decision. (1) Pg tx: does SELECT ... FOR UPDATE ORDER BY branch actually prevent the double-miss (two GCs for sibling branches on one coordinate both reading remaining>0 and neither shredding → leak)? Walk two concurrent txs step by step under READ COMMITTED: does the FOR UPDATE lock force serialization so exactly ONE observes remaining==0? Is the lock on the RIGHT rows (all rows of the coordinate, before the delete)? Could the deterministic ORDER BY still deadlock if two txs lock different coordinates that interleave? (2) the shred happens OUTSIDE/AFTER the tx (GCOverlays calls Shred after DeleteRefAndCount returns) — is there a window where remaining==0 is observed, then before Shred runs a NEW branch re-Records that ref (idempotent republish re-mints a live DEK), and then Shred deletes the now-live DEK → data loss? i.e. is the shred decision still valid at shred time, or does it need the shred inside the lock / a re-check? (3) Mem impl: delete+count under mutex — correct, but does GCOverlays hold anything across the Shred? Construct any residual leak or over-reap.` },
  { key:'correctness', prompt:`LENS: fix completeness + no new defect. (1) per-ref delete: a row recorded AFTER the Overlays() snapshot survives (not de-indexed without shred) — confirm the blanket Delete is fully gone and nothing else wipes rows. (2) fail-safe: DeleteRefAndCount error → GCOverlays returns without shredding remaining refs — but it ALREADY deleted+shredded earlier refs in the loop; is a partial GC run safe + idempotent (re-run completes the rest)? does the early return leak the already-deleted-but-unshredded state? (3) does GCOverlays still resolve repoID→slug and use the slug for BOTH the index ops AND the Shred BrainKey (consistent identity)? (4) migration 028: the new (repo_key, overlay_ref) index — valid SQL, mirrors conventions, chain valid; does the count query use it? (5) the interface change — all callers/impls/fakes updated; is Delete(slug,branch) still referenced anywhere (dangling)? (6) Shred on a coordinate whose object was already shredded (idempotent) — safe? Construct a partial-run leak, an identity mismatch, or a dangling-reference compile issue.` },
]
