// FactSetRef is the content-addressed logical ref for a facts blob: the sha256 of
// the exact plaintext NDJSON, prefixed. It is stable across re-seals (a fresh DEK
// per seal changes the ciphertext, not this plaintext-content ref) and changes iff
// the blob BYTES change. Note the ref keys on bytes, not on the logical fact-set:
// merge can serialize the same logical set in different byte order (e.g. provenance
// anchors ordered by CAS-arrival), so two members are NOT guaranteed to compute an
// identical ref for the same logical set. Convergence does not depend on that — the
// read-merge-CAS loop is idempotent under keep-both (merging only grows the set), so
// after each member advances once the set reaches a fixed point where every further
