<title>The Semantic Reasoning Layer — Roadmap</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0e0f12; --bg-2: #14151a; --panel: #17181e; --panel-2: #1c1e26;
    --line: rgba(250,250,250,.09); --line-2: rgba(250,250,250,.14);
    --ink: #f4f4f6; --ink-2: #b7b9c2; --ink-3: #7c7e8a;
    --accent: #f25333; --accent-soft: rgba(242,83,51,.14);
    --sem: #22d3ee; --fact: #fbbf24; --coord: #818cf8; --fed: #34d399; --behav: #f472b6;
    --ok: #34d399; --wip: #fbbf24; --plan: #6b6e7a;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    --sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
    --r: 12px;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :root {
      --bg:#f4f2ee; --bg-2:#ebe9e3; --panel:#fbfaf7; --panel-2:#f3f1ec;
      --line:rgba(20,18,14,.10); --line-2:rgba(20,18,14,.16);
      --ink:#1a1815; --ink-2:#4c4a44; --ink-3:#807d74;
      --accent:#d8401f; --accent-soft:rgba(216,64,31,.10);
      --sem:#0e93ad; --fact:#b07d09; --coord:#5b52d6; --fed:#0f9d63; --behav:#c43f86;
      --ok:#0f9d63; --wip:#b07d09; --plan:#8a8780;
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg:#0e0f12; --bg-2:#14151a; --panel:#17181e; --panel-2:#1c1e26;
    --line:rgba(250,250,250,.09); --line-2:rgba(250,250,250,.14);
    --ink:#f4f4f6; --ink-2:#b7b9c2; --ink-3:#7c7e8a;
    --accent:#f25333; --accent-soft:rgba(242,83,51,.14);
    --sem:#22d3ee; --fact:#fbbf24; --coord:#818cf8; --fed:#34d399; --behav:#f472b6;
    --ok:#34d399; --wip:#fbbf24; --plan:#6b6e7a;
  }
  :root[data-theme="light"] {
    --bg:#f4f2ee; --bg-2:#ebe9e3; --panel:#fbfaf7; --panel-2:#f3f1ec;
    --line:rgba(20,18,14,.10); --line-2:rgba(20,18,14,.16);
    --ink:#1a1815; --ink-2:#4c4a44; --ink-3:#807d74;
    --accent:#d8401f; --accent-soft:rgba(216,64,31,.10);
    --sem:#0e93ad; --fact:#b07d09; --coord:#5b52d6; --fed:#0f9d63; --behav:#c43f86;
    --ok:#0f9d63; --wip:#b07d09; --plan:#8a8780;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink); font-family:var(--sans); line-height:1.55;
    font-size:15px; -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased; }
  .wrap { max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; padding:44px 24px 72px; }

  /* header */
  header { border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom:26px; margin-bottom:32px; }
  .eyebrow { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11.5px; letter-spacing:.22em; text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent); font-weight:600; margin:0 0 12px; }
  h1 { font-size:clamp(28px,4.6vw,44px); line-height:1.04; letter-spacing:-.02em; margin:0 0 14px;
    text-wrap:balance; font-weight:680; }
  .lede { max-width:66ch; color:var(--ink-2); font-size:16px; margin:0; }
  .lede b { color:var(--ink); font-weight:600; }

  .tiles { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:12px; margin-top:26px; }
  .tile { background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--r); padding:14px 16px; }
  .tile .n { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:26px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.02em; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .tile .l { font-size:12px; color:var(--ink-3); margin-top:2px; }
  .tile.done .n { color:var(--ok); }

  /* rails strip */
  .rails { margin:26px 0 8px; padding:13px 16px; background:var(--bg-2); border:1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius:var(--r); font-size:13px; color:var(--ink-2); }
  .rails b { color:var(--ink); font-weight:600; }
  .rails code { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--accent); background:var(--accent-soft);
    padding:1px 6px; border-radius:5px; }

  h2.sec { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--ink-3); font-weight:600; margin:38px 0 16px; }

  /* project cards */
  .proj { display:grid; grid-template-columns:180px 1fr; gap:0; background:var(--panel);
    border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden; margin-bottom:16px; }
  @media (max-width:720px){ .proj { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  .p-head { padding:20px 18px; border-right:1px solid var(--line); position:relative;
    background:linear-gradient(180deg, var(--panel-2), var(--panel)); }
  @media (max-width:720px){ .p-head { border-right:none; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); } }
  .p-head::before { content:""; position:absolute; left:0; top:0; bottom:0; width:3px; background:var(--hue); }
  .p-code { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--hue); letter-spacing:.04em; }
  .p-name { font-size:17px; font-weight:640; letter-spacing:-.01em; margin:6px 0 10px; line-height:1.2; }
  .p-meta { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11.5px; color:var(--ink-3); }
  .p-tag { display:inline-block; margin-top:11px; font-size:11px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:.04em;
    padding:3px 9px; border-radius:999px; }
  .p-body { padding:16px 18px; }
  .p-desc { color:var(--ink-2); font-size:13.5px; margin:0 0 13px; max-width:70ch; }
  .p-desc b { color:var(--ink); font-weight:600; }

  ul.ms { list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:7px; }
  .ms li { display:grid; grid-template-columns:auto 1fr auto; gap:10px; align-items:baseline;
    padding:7px 0; border-top:1px dashed var(--line); font-size:13.5px; }
  .ms li:first-child { border-top:none; }
  .ms .mc { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--ink-3); font-weight:600; white-space:nowrap; }
  .ms .mt b { color:var(--ink); font-weight:600; }
  .ms .mt span { color:var(--ink-2); }
  .pill { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:10px; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; font-weight:700;
    padding:2px 7px; border-radius:5px; white-space:nowrap; }
  .pill.ok { color:var(--ok); background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok) 15%, transparent); }
  .pill.wip { color:var(--wip); background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--wip) 15%, transparent); }
  .pill.plan { color:var(--plan); background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--plan) 16%, transparent); }
  .dep { margin-top:12px; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11.5px; color:var(--ink-3); }
  .dep b { color:var(--ink-2); }

  /* two-up for P3/P4 */
  .duo { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:16px; }
  @media (max-width:720px){ .duo { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  .duo .proj { grid-template-columns:1fr; margin-bottom:0; }
  .duo .p-head { border-right:none; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }

  /* footer / adrs */
  .foot { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr; gap:16px; margin-top:34px; }
  @media (max-width:720px){ .foot { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  .box { background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--r); padding:18px; }
  .box h3 { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--ink-3); margin:0 0 12px; font-weight:600; }
  .adr { display:flex; gap:9px; align-items:baseline; padding:6px 0; border-top:1px dashed var(--line); font-size:13px; color:var(--ink-2); }
  .adr:first-of-type { border-top:none; }
  .adr code { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11px; color:var(--accent); white-space:nowrap; }
  .flow { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; line-height:2; color:var(--ink-2); }
  .flow b { color:var(--ink); }
  .flow .a { color:var(--accent); }

  .note { margin-top:30px; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid var(--line);
    font-size:12px; color:var(--ink-3); max-width:74ch; }
</style>

<div class="wrap">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Entire · initiative roadmap</p>
    <h1>The Semantic Reasoning Layer</h1>
    <p class="lede">Turn Entire's captured sessions and local semantic brain into a <b>shared, coordinated,
      org-wide reasoning layer</b> — from a single developer's local memory to team-synced knowledge,
      collision-free parallel agents, cross-org federation, and behavioral intelligence that routes work to
      the right agent or person. Six projects, ~124 milestone-tasks, built on entire.io's existing rails.</p>

    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile done"><div class="n">P0</div><div class="l">Local brain — GA, shipped</div></div>
      <div class="tile done"><div class="n">P1.M1</div><div class="l">Server store — built, hardened</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="n">6</div><div class="l">Projects, P0 → P5</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="n">26</div><div class="l">Milestones across the arc</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="rails">
      <b>No new infrastructure.</b> The whole arc rides entire.io's post-refactor decentralized rails:
      <code>entiredb</code> (objstore · refstore · rsl · refevents), <code>checkpoint_remote</code>,
      <code>snapshotstore</code> / <code>snapshotcrypt</code>, <code>authz</code> / SpiceDB, and the
      jurisdiction <code>forwarder</code>. Each milestone ports proven components onto the brain model rather
      than building storage or crypto from scratch.
    </div>
  </header>

  <h2 class="sec">The arc — foundation to application</h2>

  <!-- P0 -->
  <div class="proj" style="--hue:var(--fed)">
    <div class="p-head">
      <div class="p-code">P0 · 5M / 24 tasks</div>
      <div class="p-name">GA the local brain</div>
      <div class="p-meta">the foundation</div>
      <div class="p-tag" style="color:var(--ok);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ok) 15%,transparent)">SHIPPED</div>
    </div>
    <div class="p-body">
      <p class="p-desc">A tagged, version-stamped, benchmark-gated local brain. <b>entire-sem</b> (semantic
        provider) + <b>entire-brain</b> (the local brain) + <b>brain-bench</b> as a CI gate — schema
        <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">1.x</code> frozen, <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">v0.1.0</code> tagged.</p>
      <ul class="ms">
        <li><span class="mc">M1–M2</span><span class="mt"><b>Semantic GA + Phase-1 suite</b> <span>— provider parses locally, deterministic suite green on 3 OSes</span></span><span class="pill ok">done</span></li>
        <li><span class="mc">M3</span><span class="mt"><b>Reconcile + durable facts</b> <span>— distill, dedupe, branch-scoped fact store</span></span><span class="pill ok">done</span></li>
        <li><span class="mc">M4</span><span class="mt"><b>Docs + eval harness</b> <span>— facts/history eval, coverage audit</span></span><span class="pill ok">done</span></li>
        <li><span class="mc">M5</span><span class="mt"><b>brain-bench CI gate</b> <span>— 30/30 languages significant vs the reference tool; no-drift regression floor</span></span><span class="pill ok">done</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- P1 -->
  <div class="proj" style="--hue:var(--accent)">
    <div class="p-head">
      <div class="p-code">P1 · 4M / 21 tasks ★</div>
      <div class="p-name">Shared / hosted brain</div>
      <div class="p-meta">the differentiator</div>
      <div class="p-tag" style="color:var(--wip);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--wip) 15%,transparent)">M1 DONE · IN FLIGHT</div>
    </div>
    <div class="p-body">
      <p class="p-desc">Lift the brain from local-only to <b>shared and synced across a team</b>. The linchpin
        every later project depends on. Rides the mirror architecture: content-addressed CIDs, KMS-wrapped
        per-object DEKs, authz-gated, jurisdiction-routed.</p>
      <ul class="ms">
        <li><span class="mc">M1</span><span class="mt"><b>Server-side brain store</b> <span>— hosted, content-addressed, authz-gated; store · validation · encryption · durable DEK · publish endpoint · branch policy · GC</span></span><span class="pill ok">done</span></li>
        <li><span class="mc">M2</span><span class="mt"><b>Durable-fact sync + merge model</b> <span>— shared facts, conflict/merge across branches and members</span></span><span class="pill plan">planned</span></li>
        <li><span class="mc">M3</span><span class="mt"><b>Remote MCP transport</b> <span>— the brain over a network MCP, not just local stdio</span></span><span class="pill plan">planned</span></li>
        <li><span class="mc">M4</span><span class="mt"><b>Brain auth / tenancy</b> <span>— multi-tenant, SpiceDB-gated access</span></span><span class="pill plan">planned</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="dep">M1 blocks → <b>P2.M3 · P3 · P4</b>   |   M4 blocks → <b>P2.M3</b> (auth on the unified surface)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- P2 -->
  <div class="proj" style="--hue:var(--sem)">
