		// casCommandError) and a lost CREATE race as "already exists". Neither
		// matched the substrings above, so a CAS conflict fell through to a 502
		// and SKIPPED the engine's retry loop — silently dropping concurrent
		// writes. Classify both as a retryable concurrent update so the engine
		// re-fetches, replays, and (for a value-CAS) re-evaluates its
		// precondition. Substring matching is a known-fragile seam pinned to the
		// entiredb wire text; a typed CAS-conflict contract would be sturdier.
		strings.Contains(msg, "remote ref has changed") ||
		strings.Contains(msg, "already exists")
